&= {1 \over ((1+x)^{-1})^{48-k}} \\
&= {1 \over (1 - (\sqrt5+1)(\root 4\of5+1)(\root 8\of5+1)(\root {16}\of5+1) + \cdots)^{-(48-k)}}
\end{align}

Now, you can calculate the fourth power of \((x+1)^{48}\) using the Binomial Theorem and find the sum of all the \((x^{48-k}) \times \left(\frac{1}{(1 - (\sqrt5+1)(\root 4\of5+1)(\root 8\of5+1)(\root {16}\of5+1) + \cdots)^{-(48-k)}}\right)\) terms.

