To find the equivalent number of wands in terms of fands, we will cross-multiply the ratios provided, which results in:

\begin{align*}
\frac{4\text{ wands}}{6\text{ rands}} \times \frac{24\text{ rands}}{8\text{ fands}} &= \frac{4 \times 24}{6 \times 8} \text{ wands per fand } \\
