&= 1 \text{ wand per fand}
\end{align*}

Given that 1 wand is equal to 1 fand, to find the equivalent number of wands for 5 fands, simply multiply the two quantities.

\boxed{5\text{ fands} \times 1 \text{ wand per fand }= \boxed{5\text{ wands }}}

