Since she has less than 10 dollars worth of quarters, we know that Q < 10*25, implying that Q < 250.

Let's find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of x and y, which will give us the largest possible common multiple for the two denominators of the fractions 5Q - 3 and 7Q - 5.

\gcd(x, y) = \gcd(5Q - 3, 7Q - 5)

