The volume of a cube is given by the formula $V = s^3$, where $s$ is the length of an edge.

If the volume is increased by 19 cubic centimeters, the new volume $V_n$ is given by $V_n = V_1 + 19$, where $V_1$ is the original volume.

First, find the original volume $V_1$:

\begin{align*}
V_1 &= s^3 \\
       &= (2\text{ cm})^3 \\
       &= 8\text{ cubic cm}
\end{align*}

Next, find the new volume:

\begin{align*}
V_n &= V_1 + 19 \\
       &=8\text{ cubic cm} + 19\text{ cubic cm} \\
       &= 27\text{ cubic cm}
\end{align*}

Since the volume is a cube, the sides of the new cube have been increased by a factor of $\sqrt[3]{3}$. Multiplying the original edge length $s$ by this factor gives the edge length of the new cube, $s_n$:

\begin{align*}
s_n &= s * \sqrt[3]{3} \\
       &= 2\text{ cm } * \sqrt[3]{3} \\
       &= \boxed{ 2\sqrt[3]{3} \text{ cm } }
\end{align*}

The answer is 2 times the cube root of three, which is approximately 4.2599 Centimeters, but as you asked for exact values, the final answer should not include approximation as per the given problem statement.

